 or vitamin C can help lighten dark spots and even out the skin tone.\n- **Results take time.** One source says a 2015 study found salicylic acid highly effective at reducing the appearance of dark patches when used consistently over 2-3 months. A brightening deodorant review says its product is designed to work gradually, yielding visible brightening over several weeks.\n- **Some causes aren't avoidable.** One dermatologist notes that in many cases, dark armpits are hereditary and can't be avoided, though reducing shaving irritation still lowers the risk.\n\nMost of these sources are brand-affiliated, so the product claims in particular deserve skepticism. If you want the user-experience angle you searched for, a Reddit-specific query (for example, naming r/SkincareAddiction or r/AsianBeauty) may turn up threads."],"durationSeconds":6.180642667,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Dz1M6D5vdySbbkqq1MR7vv","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
