WK7Z9vfaHBnrzTcFWGs3","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013aQFFKNdnPZCB1hHc4dWNA","type":"tool_result","content":"**Prevalence and population**\n- The article doesn't give a prevalence figure for axillary hyperpigmentation specifically. It cites an international survey estimating that post-inflammatory hyperpigmentation (PIH) affects almost 15% of people, more often women.\n- Axillary hyperpigmentation is described as especially common in women with darker skin. Most included studies enrolled women with Fitzpatrick types III to V.\n\n**Causes**\n- The authors consider it a form of PIH, driven by irritation and inflammation from friction, hair plucking, shaving, deodorants, and whitening agents.\n- The axilla has more sebaceous and sweat glands and hair follicles, and higher water loss, which the authors say weakens its skin barrier.\n- Other causes such as erythrasma, freckling, neurofibromatosis type 1, and acanthosis nigricans should be ruled out first.\n\n**Topical treatments with evidence**\n- **Niacinamide (4%):** One randomized trial of 24 women found it beat placebo. Good-to-excellent response was 24%, versus 6% with placebo, after 9 weeks, with no adverse effects reported. Desonide 0.05% did better (30%).\n- **Other agents studied:** Cyperus rotundus oil, hydroquinone, glycolic acid, alpha hydroxy acid (AHA), a Perilla frutescens serum, sweet orange peel cream, and a novel serum. Desonide and C. rotundus oil showed the strongest results in the authors' summary.\n- **Not covered:** The article does not evaluate licorice or lactic acid. Arbutin appears only as an ingredient in a comparator cream, not as a studied treatment.\n\n**Typical treatment durations**\n- Topical studies: about 4 weeks (Perilla serum), 8 weeks (sweet orange cream; glycolic acid case series), 9 weeks (niacinamide and desonide), 12 weeks (C. rotundus oil and hydroquinone), and 90 days (a serum-versus-cream comparison).\n- Laser and light: sessions every 2 weeks, with 3 to 12 sessions for Q-switched Nd:YAG and 5 sessions for IPL.\n- The authors note that PIH treatment can last up to 8 years, but this is a general PIH figure.\n\n**Caveats**\nThe authors state that the evidence is limited, mostly small studies with short follow-up, and that no standard treatment exists. They also could not perform a meta-analysis."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"68c9f62a-b8d7-4f1b-9daf-d55be40f8038","uuid":"878c2cf1-4b1c-4d20-858a-ad65602566de","timestamp":"2026-11-28T11:24:23.696Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":187820,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"**Prevalence and population**\n- The article doesn't give a prevalence figure for axillary hyperpigmentation specifically. It cites an international survey estimating that post-inflammatory hyperpigmentation (PIH) affects almost 15% of people, more often women.\n- Axillary hyperpigmentation is described as especially common in women with darker skin. Most included studies enrolled women with Fitzpatrick types III to V.\n\n**Causes**\n- The authors consider it a form of PIH, driven by irritation and inflammation from friction, hair plucking, shaving, deodorants, and whitening agents.\n- The axilla has more sebaceous and sweat glands and hair follicles, and higher water loss, which the authors say weakens its skin barrier.\n- Other causes such as erythrasma, freckling, neurofibromatosis type 1, and acanthosis nigricans should be ruled out first.\n\n**Topical treatments with evidence**\n- **Niacinamide (4%):** One randomized trial of 24 women found it beat placebo. Good-to-excellent response was 24%, versus 6% with placebo, after 9 weeks, with no adverse effects reported. Desonide 0.05% did better (30%).\n- **Other agents studied:** Cyperus rotundus oil, hydroquinone, glycolic acid, alpha hydroxy acid (AHA), a Perilla frutescens serum, sweet orange peel cream, and a novel serum. Desonide and C. rotundus oil showed the strongest results in the authors' summary.\n- **Not covered:** The article does not evaluate licorice or lactic acid. Arbutin appears only as an ingredient in a comparator cream, not as a studied treatment.\n\n**Typical treatment durations**\n- Topical studies: about 4 weeks (Perilla serum), 8 weeks (sweet orange cream; glycolic acid case series), 9 weeks (niacinamide and desonide), 12 weeks (C. rotundus oil and hydroquinone), and 90 days (a serum-versus-cream comparison).\n- Laser and light: sessions every 2 weeks, with 3 to 12 sessions for Q-switched Nd:YAG and 5 sessions for IPL.\n- The authors note that PIH treatment can last up to 8 years, but this is a general PIH figure.\n\n**Caveats**\nThe authors state that the evidence is limited, mostly small studies with short follow-up, and that no standard treatment exists. They also could not perform a meta-analysis.","durationMs":9048,"url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12371607/"},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_013aQFFKNdnPZCB1hHc4dWNA","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WRRexmq9WAMVpTQ5KDghAm","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"comercio electrónico Colombia 2026 pago contra entrega porcentaje compras belleza cuidado personal\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"emprendedores experimentan alza de 136 en ventas online 574865\",\"url\":\"https://www.portafolio.co/negocios/emprendimiento/emprendedores-experimentan-alza-de-136-en-ventas-online-574865\"},{\"title\":\"Publico V1 2026 IInforme 1er trimestre economico\",\"url\":\"https://ccce.org.co/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Publico_V1-2026-IInforme-1er-trimestre-economico.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"articles 438903 Article\",\"url\":\"https://observatorioecommerce.mintic.gov.co/797/articles-438903_Article.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"articles 438819 Article\",\"url\":\"https://observatorioecommerce.mintic.gov.co/797/articles-438819_Article.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"articles 439986 Article\",\"url\":\"https://observatorioecommerce.mintic.gov.co/797/articles-439986_Article.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Ecommerce en Colombia: ¿cómo aprovechar su crecimiento?\",\"url\":\"https://www.tiendanube.com/blog/ecommerce-colombia/\"},{\"title\":\"Ecommerce en Colombia: ¿cómo aprovechar su crecimiento?\",\"url\":\"https://www.tiendanube.com/co/blog/ecommerce-colombia\"},{\"title\":\"Arquitectura de pagos para e-commerce en Colombia: cómo combinar digital, contraentrega y recaudo inteligente\",\"url\":\"https://encolombia.com/?p=392285\"},{\"title\":\"Comercio electrónico\",\"url\":\"https://www.noticiasrcn.com/temas/comercio-electronico\"},{\"title\":\"repository.icesi.edu.co\",\"url\":\"https://repository.icesi.edu.co/bitstreams/0eb8e37f-c868-4d49-ac1f-e6c11c7ab242/download\"},{\"title\":\"comercio electronico en colombia 2026 guia para empezar\",\"url\":\"https://www.andreybusiness.com/blog/comercio-electronico-en-colombia-2026-guia-para-empezar\"},{\"title\":\"articles 439987 Article\",\"url\":\"https://observatorioecommerce.mintic.gov.co/797/articles-439987_Article.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"articles 428123 Article\",\"url\":\"https://observatorioecommerce.mintic.gov.co/797/articles-428123_Article.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"V2 1 PUBLICO INFORME DE CIERRE 2025\",\"url\":\"https://ccce.org.co/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/V2-1-PUBLICO-INFORME-DE-CIERRE-2025.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"La Nota Económica\",\"url\":\"https://lanotaeconomica.com.co/?p=17823\"},{\"title\":\"cuanto gastan los colombianos en belleza y cuidado personal 207059\",\"url\":\"https://www.elheraldo.co/tendencias/2015/07/23/cuanto-gastan-los-colombianos-en-belleza-y-cuidado-personal-207059/\"},{\"title\":\"que parte de las compras online va de vuelta a la tienda 4423630\",\"url\":\"https://www.larepublica.co/consumo/que-parte-de-las-compras-online-va-de-vuelta-a-la-tienda-4423630\"},{\"title\":\"crecen las ventas online en colombia camara de comercio electronico entrego cifras 1745\",\"url\":\"https://www.elpais.com.co/economia/crecen-las-ventas-online-en-colombia-camara-de-comercio-electronico-entrego-cifras-1745.html\"}]\n\nNo encontré una cifra de 2026 sobre el porcentaje de compras en belleza y cuidado personal pagadas contra entrega. Las fuentes que hay son de distintos años y se contradicen en el peso de este método de pago.\n\n- **Contra entrega según datos oficiales:** Un análisis del MinTIC con datos de la Cámara Colombiana de Comercio Electrónico (CCCE) indica que el efectivo, incluido el pago contra entrega, bajó del 5,2% al 2,7% entre 2022 y 2025. Un artículo de Tiendanube sobre el segundo trimestre de 2026 ubica el efectivo, incluidos los pagos en puntos de recaudo o contra entrega, en 2,7%.\n- **Cifra contradictoria:** Un blog de dropshipping, que promueve una plataforma, afirma que el contra entrega representa el 70-80% de las ventas en comercio electrónico colombiano. Esta cifra no tiene fuente verificable y conflicta con los datos de la CCCE, así que no conviene usarla.\n- **Belleza y cuidado personal:** Un artículo de Portafolio, sin fecha clara en el resultado, reporta que belleza y cuidado personal, con un 31,3% son las categorías que más comercializan los emprendedores en sus tiendas virtuales. Ese mismo artículo indica que la mayoría de los usuarios de una plataforma prefieren el pago contra entrega por encima de cualquier otro método, aunque ese dato proviene de una declaración de la empresa, no de un estudio general.\n- **Ventas totales 2026:** Según la CCCE, en 2025, las ventas online en Colombia alcanzaron $145,4 billones. Para el segundo trimestre de 2026, Tiendanube reporta COP $26,9 billones entre abril y junio de 2026, un aumento del 3% con respecto al año anterior.\n\nPara una cifra precisa de belleza y cuidado personal con contra entrega en 2026, habría que consultar directamente los informes trimestrales de la CCCE o el Observatorio de Comercio Electrónico del MinTIC, que desglosan categorías y medios de pago.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"68c9f62a-b8d7-4f1b-9daf-d55be40f8038","uuid":"8e950af1-af06-400e-8431-889d1b3e3983","timestamp":"2026-11-28T11:24:24.316Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"comercio electrónico Colombia 2026 pago contra entrega porcentaje compras belleza cuidado personal","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01DUb12ekuQyJes8AHGW94pp","content":[{"title":"emprendedores experimentan alza de 136 en ventas online 574865","url":"https://www.portafolio.co/negocios/emprendimiento/emprendedores-experimentan-alza-de-136-en-ventas-online-574865"},{"title":"Publico V1 2026 IInforme 1er trimestre economico","url":"https://ccce.org.co/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Publico_V1-2026-IInforme-1er-trimestre-economico.pdf"},{"title":"articles 438903 Article","url":"https://observatorioecommerce.mintic.gov.co/797/articles-438903_Article.pdf"},{"title":"articles 438819 Article","url":"https://observatorioecommerce.mintic.gov.co/797/articles-438819_Article.pdf"},{"title":"articles