he-vitamin-c-13-serum/\"},{\"title\":\"Even Up® Multi-Correction Serum\",\"url\":\"https://www.colorescience.com/products/even-up-multi-correction-serum\"},{\"title\":\"Arbonne Intelligence Genius Nightly Resurfacing Pads & Solution\",\"url\":\"https://skinsort.com/products/arbonne/intelligence-genius-nightly-resurfacing-pads-solution\"},{\"title\":\"turmeric tonic\",\"url\":\"https://www.cocokind.com/collections/face/products/turmeric-tonic\"},{\"title\":\"patchology hero status roll model brightening roll on eye serum\",\"url\":\"https://www.belleandblush.com/collections/all/products/patchology-hero-status-roll-model-brightening-roll-on-eye-serum\"}]\n\nI couldn't find Amazon reviews for the Nu Skin Scion roll-on, and the results don't say anything about stains, smell, or sensitive-skin reactions for this product.\n\nThe closest match is a Female Daily listing for the Scion Whitening Roll-On Deodorant. It shows an average of about 4.5 stars from roughly 678 users, and 98% users Recommended this. That page is a beauty-review site, not Amazon, and it is not clear how many of those users were reviewing from the same market. One reviewer who had used it for over a year doesn't recommend this product, but the snippet gives no reason.\n\nThe other results cover different products, such as a different roll-on from ODDLY and a Tend Skin serum. Their reviews mention strong smells and staining, but those products aren't the Scion roll-on. If you need the Amazon-specific picture, search Amazon directly, filtering for \"stain,\" \"smell,\" or \"sensitive\" in the review text.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"68c9f62a-b8d7-4f1b-9daf-d55be40f8038","uuid":"4df6df71-61b4-4977-bec3-7a58f07de08a","timestamp":"2026-11-28T11:24:34.610Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Nu Skin Scion brightening roll-on amazon reviews stains smell sensitive skin","results":[{"tool_use_id":"s